@startuml sequence_diagram_date_filtering

actor User
participant "TodoCLI / Menu" as CLI
participant "TodoService" as Service
participant "TaskManager" as Manager

autonumber

User -> CLI: list --week 2026-W20
CLI -> CLI: parse YYYY-Www format
CLI -> Service: list_tasks_by_week(2026, 20, status)
Service -> Manager: _get_week_boundaries(2026, 20)
Manager -> Manager: Calculate Monday (ISO day 1) and Sunday (ISO day 7)
Manager -> Service: Return (week_start, week_end)
Service -> Manager: list_by_due_date_range(after=week_start, before=week_end, status=status)
Manager -> Manager: Filter tasks by due_date range
Manager -> Service: Return filtered tasks
Service -> CLI: Return task list
CLI -> User: Display tasks

autonumber

User -> CLI: list --month 2026-05
CLI -> CLI: parse YYYY-MM format
CLI -> Service: list_tasks_by_month(2026, 5, status)
Service -> Manager: _get_month_boundaries(2026, 5)
Manager -> Manager: Calculate 1st and last day of month
Manager -> Service: Return (month_start, month_end)
Service -> Manager: list_by_due_date_range(after=month_start, before=month_end, status=status)
Manager -> Manager: Filter tasks by due_date range
Manager -> Service: Return filtered tasks
Service -> CLI: Return task list
CLI -> User: Display tasks

autonumber

User -> CLI: list --due-before 2026-05-15T23:59:59+00:00 --due-after 2026-05-01T00:00:00+00:00
CLI -> CLI: Parse ISO 8601 date strings
CLI -> Service: list_tasks(before=2026-05-15T23:59:59, after=2026-05-01T00:00:00, status=status, overdue_only=false)
Service -> Manager: list_by_due_date_range(before=..., after=..., status=..., overdue_only=...)
Manager -> Manager: Filter tasks by date range and status
Manager -> Service: Return filtered tasks
Service -> CLI: Return task list
CLI -> User: Display tasks

autonumber

User -> CLI: list --overdue
CLI -> Service: list_tasks(overdue_only=true)
Service -> Manager: list_by_due_date_range(overdue_only=true)
Manager -> Manager: Filter only overdue tasks (due_date < now and status != DONE)
Manager -> Service: Return filtered tasks
Service -> CLI: Return task list
CLI -> User: Display tasks

@enduml
